      "writtenOn": "2023-04-10T15:46:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That makes sense. It really does only make sense for types that don\u0027t have padding, which is then pretty coupled back to the wrapper around the span knowing what it\u0027s doing. I can get rid of the span overloads.\n\nWDYT about the other restructuring though? This lets types define their hash specializations more conveniently IMO, but maybe it\u0027s better to be explicit about declaring a type as `Map\u003cK, V, K::Hash\u003e` vs. there being a specialization for `SkGoodHash\u003cK\u003e` floating around and the user declaring `Map\u003cK, V\u003e`?",
      "parentUuid": "7c5d641c_0003fae3",
      "revId": "5e6cf9a86c1454cfc3a878ce9038a4f8da873a9e",
