      "writtenOn": "2023-04-10T17:38:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That makes sense. So no explicit specialization for `SkSpan\u003cK\u003e`. For correctness, we should have the existing templates for single key values still use `std::has_unique_object_representations`.\n\nThe question that remains is for classes that define a custom hash function (such as for the wrapper around a span that knows it\u0027s immutable, or where it needs the flexibility), do we just keep it as-is? The class exposes a Hash struct that users need to include in maps? Or do we switch to a more `std::hash` function object approach?",
      "parentUuid": "5bf709e3_a2d97e0c",
